description:
Binance is a leading global blockchain ecosystem behind the world’s largest cryptocurrency exchange by trading volume and registered users. We are trusted by 300+ million people in 100+ countries for our industry-leading security, user fund transparency, trading engine speed, deep liquidity, and an unmatched portfolio of digital-asset products. Binance offerings range from trading and finance to education, research, payments, institutional services, and more. Our mission is to increase the freedom of money and financial access for people around the world.

Responsibilities

• Support the rollout and implementation of 2C AI product features;

• Translate product requirements from stakeholders into clear execution plans and documentation;

• Work closely with engineering, design, marketing, and operations teams to support delivery;

• Track progress, manage timelines, and help resolve execution issues;

• Monitor feature performance and collect user feedback for future improvements;

• Support pilot launches, global rollouts, multilingual expansion, and ongoing optimization;

• Help improve user experience by identifying issues and sharing suggestions with stakeholders.

Qualifications

• 3–4 years of experience in project management, product operations, or a related role;

• Experience supporting consumer-facing AI products is preferred;

• Strong execution skills and ability to manage cross-functional projects;

• Comfortable working in a fast-paced, high-pressure environment;

• Able to handle launch pressure and user feedback professionally;

• Strong communication and stakeholder management skills;

• Growth mindset, high EQ, and strong ownership.

Why Binance

• Shape the future of finance

• Collaborate with world-class talent in a user-centric global organization with a flat structure

• Tackle challenging projects in a fast-paced and innovative enviornment with autonomy

• Thrive in a results-driven workplace with opportunities for career growth and continuous learning

• Competitive salary and company benefits

• Remote-first, work-from-home arrangement (may vary depending on the nature of the role and team)

Binance is committed to being an equal opportunity employer. We believe that having a diverse workforce is fundamental to our success.

By submitting a job application, you acknowledge that you have read our Candidate Privacy Notice .

We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.

1. JOB DESCRIPTION
Job Title
Service Technician
Occupation
MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT TECHNICIAN
Job Description & Requirements
Service Technician
Company Overview:
Cleantools is the leader in cleaning solutions & systems in Singapore.
We develop , manufacture, and distribute premium products and cleaning systems for the European, Southeast Asian, Chinese, and UK markets.
From cleaning machines & equipment to automatic robots & accessories, we always value sustainable relations with our clients and partners by providing bespoke products & services. Cleaning is our passion! We are always excited to share this knowledge through our expertise & experience. We are looking for a strongly motivated and skilled individual to be a part of this dynamic industry.

Join us

• 5 days' work week

• Conducive working environment.

• Training will be provided

• Salary will commensurate according to experience & qualifications

Job Scope

• Provides on-site and in-house after-sales support;

• Rectify and repair faults of various cleaning equipment and tools, (e.g. vacuum cleaners, scrubbers, blowers);

• Maintain condition of various larger cleaning equipment (e.g. Scrubber driers, road sweepers);

• Troubleshoot and perform on job rectification works for clients;

• Demonstrate and train clients on the use of the various machines;

• Deploy robotic cleaning machines to various sites and provide testing and training to clients;

• Ad-hoc duties as assigned.

Requirements

• Minimum Nitec / Higher Nitec in Electrical & Mechanical engineering related discipline;

• 2 years of hands-on experience is preferred;

• Possesses basic electrical Know-how;

• Possession of a Class 3 driving license;

• Good team player who can work well with others;

• Able to communicate in both English and Mandarin (essential for liaison and communication with our China-based counterparts)

•

Working Conditions:

• · Operation hours: 8.30 am – 6.00 pm (Monday – Friday).

• · Working location: Kaki Bukit / Eunos Link.

• · Dress Code: Casual (e.g., Polo-Tee /business shirt).

Job Description & Requirements

Key Responsibilities

During the rotation, you will be involved in the following areas:

1. Marketing & Brand Development

- Assist in formulating marketing strategies and executing brand promotion campaigns;

- Contribute to content creation, design, and publishing across digital channels;

- Support market research and competitor analysis.

2. Student Services & Operational Support

- Help coordinate academic scheduling, student logistics, and event operations;

- Participate in optimizing service processes and enhancing customer satisfaction;

- Support administrative systems and internal communication.

3. Sales & Client Engagement

- Assist in handling client inquiries, course recommendations, and customer onboarding;

- Contribute to refining sales strategies and improving conversion efficiency;

- Manage and analyze CRM data to support sales initiatives.

4. Project Management & Cross-functional Collaboration

- Participate in internal projects under the guidance of senior mentors;

- Collaborate across departments to support business goals and process improvement;

- Provide timely updates and reports on assigned tasks and initiatives.

Requirements

- Bachelor’s degree in any discipline; fresh graduates are welcome;

- Proficient in English (both spoken and written);

- Conversational Mandarin required to liaise with Chinese-speaking clients;

- Strong interpersonal and communication skills with a collaborative mindset;

- Detail-oriented, organized, and able to manage multiple tasks under pressure;

- Positive, adaptable attitude with a strong willingness to learn and grow;

- Proficient in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint);

- Proficiency in Canva or similar graphic design tools is preferred;

- Video editing skills (e.g., CapCut, Adobe Premiere, JianYing, etc.) are a strong advantage;

- Previous internship or experience in education, marketing, or client services is a plus.
